71
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,960
I don't think this is a good idea.

72
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,760
What's wrong with it?

73
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:37,560
Shout it!

74
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,200
I... I'm horny, and I'm proud.

75
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,320
Louder!

76
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:50,360
I'm horny, and I'm proud!

77
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,320
Louder!

78
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,200
I'm horny, and I'm proud!

79
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,400
I'm horny, and I'm proud!

80
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:57,400
I'm horny, and I'm proud!

81
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,930
That's more like it.

82
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,760
Men have the autonomy to accept

83
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:02,480
and release their desires.

84
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,010
We women should have it too.

85
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,800
You need to accept yourself

86
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,260
and release your desires.

87
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,580
Don't forget to send me the photos

88
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,530
of the sea of clouds.

89
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,880
Dear player Yun Huhu,

90
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:35,920
congratulations on being selected

91
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:38,440
to participate in
this puzzle treasure hunt.

92
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,840
The first puzzle piece of this event
has been refreshed.

93
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,700
The specific location is
at the top of Mount Tianmu.

94
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:46,300
You can claim it
after watching the sunrise.

95
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,730
Just say it if you can't climb anymore.

96
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,800
Don't underestimate me.

97
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,240
Mount Tianmu is

98
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,140
a piece of cake.

99
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,000
Are you tired?

100
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,000
Not tired,

101
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,800
but I'm a little thirsty.

102
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:30,610
We're here, we're here.

103
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,130
Let's take a rest first.

104
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,440
I can't do this at all.

105
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,570
Give it to me.

106
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:44,640
Thank you.

107
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:54,010
Drink some electrolyte water.

108
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,200
Lime flavor. It's so good.

109
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:02,880
Of course.

110
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:03,720
It has

111
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,520
a new type of nutrient solution

112
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,440
called PQQ added to it.

113
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:08,440
It's refreshing and relieves fatigue.

114
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,240
No wonder.

115
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,440
I feel energetic all over
after drinking it.

116
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:11,360
I'm revived.

117
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,440
My melon.

118
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:24,800
Why did you bring such a big watermelon
to climb a mountain?

119
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:25,680
Are you crazy?

120
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,240
What do you know?

121
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,160
This is my professional energy supply.

122
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,000
If you haven't experienced the bitterness
of carrying a heavy load,

123
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,120
how can you taste the sweetness of
a watermelon at the top of the mountain?

124
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:36,240
Spend less time on the internet.

125
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,760
What a pity.

126
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,159
Let's go.

127
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:45,720
I'll pull you.

128
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,440
I can't.

129
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,440
I really can't take another step.

130
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:53,770
Let's rest a bit longer.

131
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,340
Don't you exercise at all?

132
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:58,760
I do cardio every single day.

133
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:00,380
Breathing doesn't count.

134
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:02,240
Breathing 24 hours a day

135
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,900
is already impressive, okay?

136
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,640
I really can't walk anymore.

137
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,080
Go on without me.

138
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:11,040
But

139
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,120
could you do me a favor

140
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,360
and give me the puzzle?

141
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,680
No. It's getting dark soon.

142
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:18,800
It's dangerous on the mountain.

143
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:19,320
I don't want

144
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,380
to see you on the local news tomorrow.

145
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,760
I'll carry you on my back.

146
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:30,720
Come on up.

147
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:32,280
If you don't, I'm leaving.

148
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,240
Can you handle it?

149
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,400
Don't push yourself.

150
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:36,400
Who's like you,

151
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,679
sitting in an office all day,

152
00:08:37,679 --> 00:08:38,799
weak and fragile?

153
00:08:38,799 --> 00:08:39,559
Come on.

154
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,600
Isn't that the fault of evil capitalists?

155
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,360
Trading our time for KPIs.

156
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,120
I don't have time to work out.

157
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:49,740
I'm coming.

158
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,200
I'm really coming.

159
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,040
Just come on.

160
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:58,000
Cane, cane, cane.

161
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,040
Let's go.

162
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:09,720
Run!

163
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:10,980
Run! It's raining.

164
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:16,560
Why the sudden downpour?

165
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,000
Can we still see the sunrise?

166
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,330
The forecast just said there's a typhoon.

167
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,080
I guess

168
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:22,640
it's gonna rain for a while.

169
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,000
This sucks.

170
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,080
Then what was the point

171
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,120
of climbing all the way up here?

172
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:31,520
Even if I have the energy,

173
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,360
I wore

174
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:34,280
my new clothes and shoes

175
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,000
just for this hike.

176
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:37,520
Now they're all soaked.

177
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:38,480
And

178
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,920
look at my hair.

179
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,010
I just washed it last night.

180
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:45,120
To get ready for bed,

181
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,280
I went to sleep

182
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:47,610
at 7:00 p.m. last night.

183
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,610
I went to bed early for nothing.

184
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,130
Clothes and shoes can be washed again.

185
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,120
People are waterproof.

186
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,920
It doesn't matter if you get wet.

187
00:09:58,360 --> 00:09:59,560
Let's sit for a while.

188
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:06,640
It's true.

189
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:09,520
The more you expect,
the more disappointed you get.

190
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,520
The harder you try,
the unluckier you become.

191
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:13,240
No matter what I do,

192
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,800
it's always a trial.

193
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:16,640
A trial?

194
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,420
Free trials are great,

195
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,000
right?

196
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:25,000
Is this the time for jokes?

197
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,720
Forget it. I can't explain it to you.

198
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,020
As for the sunrise,

199
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,320
if we can't see it today,

200
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,960
we can always see it tomorrow.

201
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,290
The sun is always there.

202
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:37,240
You just need to look up
whenever you want to see it.

203
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:41,720
But

204
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:46,160
playing the violin in the rain
isn't something you see every day, right?

205
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,760
What kind of normal person
brings a violin up a mountain?

206
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,200
Are you out of your...

207
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,520
You carried a watermelon up here.

208
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:00,720
We're just

209
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:02,290
fellow weirdos at best.

210
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:06,760
Here we go.

211
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:14,680
Come on, Qingqing. Don't be upset.

212
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:26,360
You're right.

213
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,290
People are waterproof.

214
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,280
Life is 70% off.

215
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:35,280
So cheap.

216
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:37,040
Soaked like a drowned chicken.

217
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:40,200
So delicious.
